{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider clears the identity limb of her burden under POL-RD-08: the trip_record, the gps_trace and the fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00526, and trip_record.started_at (2026-09-14T23:36:40+08:00) coincides with the trace's first fix, so the three artifacts describe one and the same trip and the ride can be measured on the record as it stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00526", "EV-GPS-00526", "EV-FARE-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trace is complete: 169 fixes at a 10-second cadence, coverage_pct 100.0, an empty gaps list and max_gap_sec 0.0, so it satisfies none of the impairment limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07. The rider's case therefore cannot be answered with a data-failure defence, and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises out of this trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile carries no citable adverse signal: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 condition that would require corroboration beyond the gps_trace (four or more claims with one or fewer substantiated) simply does not fire, and no other field on this profile may be used against the rider under POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the bundle can excuse any part of what the rider was charged. There is no traffic advisory at all: EV-ADVIS-00526-01 is MISSING, status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so no advisory names a road the optimal route traverses and the POL-RD-03 exoneration route is closed. The trip's chat log is likewise empty (message_count 0), so no rider-requested detour exists to invoke under POL-RD-04. I disclose the missing advisory's weight of 0.0 as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; its absence is itself citable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00526-01", "EV-CHAT-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The heart of the rider's complaint is the pricing mode, and the platform's own record proves it: trip_record.optimal_route_source records that the rider 'selected RYDE_X, display \"up to 26.00\"' and that the platform dispatched RYDE_TAXI, while the fare_breakdown records fare_model METERED on rate card RC-SG-2026Q3-RYDETAXI with quoted_fare_sgd null, and the chat log holds no message evidencing any agreement to a metered taxi. The rider chose a product shown with a maximum price and was priced on a taxi meter she never selected. She does not assert a material distance deviation — the trace excess is 0.17 km, about 1.09%, under the POL-RD-01 gate — but the metered basis itself is what she disputes, and under POL-RD-11 the fare model governs which remedy is even available.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00526", "EV-FARE-00526", "EV-CHAT-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The two fare-model routes in this policy cannot be run cleanly on this record, which is precisely the situation POL-RD-10 exists for. POL-RD-11 requires fare_breakdown.quoted_fare_sgd to be non-null and it is null, so the clause is invoked against a cited artifact that lacks the field the clause requires; POL-RD-02 runs only on a METERED trip once a deviation is established; and the record simultaneously supports a capped RYDE_X selection and a metered RYDE_TAXI dispatch, two mutually contradictory accounts of what was bought. With the required field absent and the evidence contradictory, and with no confident ruling available on the pricing basis, the case must ESCALATE under POL-RD-10, with the disputed amount held rather than collected.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00526", "EV-TRIP-00526"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and Driver — this dispute is decided on the platform's own trip records, and no money moves.\n\n1) No route deviation. The governing GPS trace records 15.77 km (EV-GPS-00526) against a booked optimal route of 15.6 km (EV-TRIP-00526) between the same pickup and drop-off. That is an excess of 0.17 km, or 1.09%. POL-RD-01 requires an excess both greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% before a deviation is established. Neither gate is met, so no deviation exists and POL-RD-02, the optimal-route fare recomputation, never runs. The trace is also unimpaired on this trip: 169 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, an empty gap list and max_gap_sec 0.0, so this is not a data-failure case and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation follows from the trace. For completeness only, had a deviation existed, the recomputed fare would have been SGD 22.46 against the SGD 24.29 charged, a difference of SGD 1.85 (well under the 90% full-refund share) — but that computation is not reached.\n\n2) No billing-integrity defect. The SGD 24.29 charged (EV-FARE-00526) is base fare 3.80 + distance fare 11.85 + time fare 7.84 + platform fee 0.80, all on metered rate card RC-SG-2026Q3-RYDETAXI. ERP and tolls are 0.00 with no gantries, and there is no airport surcharge. There is no phantom line for POL-RD-09(4) to refund, and therefore no 'billing integrity' referral.\n\n3) Rider's product point. I accept the facts you relied on: the trip record shows you selected RYDE_X with the display 'up to 26.00' and that the platform dispatched RYDE_TAXI (EV-TRIP-00526), while the ledger prices the trip on the meter (fare_model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null, EV-FARE-00526). But the fare you were charged, SGD 24.29, is below the SGD 26.00 maximum you say you chose, so there is no overcharge on this trip to refund; and the figure of SGD 46.50 in your claim appears in no record. POL-RD-11 governs capped/upfront-quoted fares and applies only where fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd is non-null. This trip was metered, so POL-RD-11 is inapplicable and supplies no remedy. It is not 'a clause invoked against an artifact lacking the field it requires' within POL-RD-10(5): it fails on the fare model itself, so no escalation follows from it.\n\n4) Rider's escalation argument rejected. The POL-RD-10 triggers do not fire: the trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and ledger; the timestamps are consistent; the trace is unimpaired; no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing or field-deficient artifact (no party asserts a traffic cause, the chat log is empty, and no amendment is claimed); and there is no pair of admissible, mutually contradictory accounts of comparable strength — the driver's statement that the meter is the fare and that the platform sent the booking is consistent with the ledger. Confidence here is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. This is a case to decide, not to hold.\n\n5) Driver's points. I accept that no repeat-deviation pattern is established: deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d of 250, so POL-RD-06 gives no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not used against anyone; it is context only under POL-GEN-01. I also accept that the rider's identity limb under POL-RD-08 is met, that her profile carries no citable adverse signal, and that no traffic advisory exists to excuse any part of the route.\n\nOutcome. The route-deviation claim is not supported by the evidence, the fare charged is below the cap the rider cites, and no clause of the route-deviation policy provides a refund on these facts. The present state stands: payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are left as they are. If the rider wishes to pursue the separate question whether the platform should have honoured the RYDE_X product she selected rather than dispatching a taxi, that is a product-substitution matter outside this policy and is not resolved here."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00526-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload, an absence that is itself citable. But no party has asserted an external traffic cause — the driver's statement is that the meter is the fare and the platform sent the booking, not that a road was closed. POL-RD-13 therefore does not engage, POL-RD-03 is not in play, and no amended optimal is substituted: the booked optimal of 15.6 km stands. Because no exculpatory clause is invoked against that absent artifact, POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered by it either.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00526-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
